        "content_text": "Jumping spiders caught on camera sleeping and leg twitching like humans.\n\n<a href=\"https://www.abc.net.au/news/science/2026-10-27/jumping-spider-rem-sleep/107309370\">The most comprehensive study of its kind confirms that jumping spiders go through two phases of sleep, including a REM-like state that is associated with human dreaming</a>.",
