        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/02/john-ternus-addresses-iphone-duo-supply-constraints-display-issue/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/john-ternus-iphone-duo-introduction.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today Apple <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/02/apple-reports-q4-2026-earnings/\">reported record Q4 earnings</a>, which beat Wall Street expectations overall. And in an <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/apple-results-beat-wall-street-expectations-on-strong-iphone-sales-2026-11-02/\">interview with <em>Reuters</em></a>, CEO John Ternus addressed current iPhone Duo supply constraints and also referenced units that have been returned for display issues.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"iphone-duo,john-ternus\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1077058\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/02/john-ternus-addresses-iphone-duo-supply-constraints-display-issue/#more-1077058\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
