        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/29/apple-says-its-only-getting-started-updating-macos-for-touchscreens/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/10/macbook-pro-proled-xdr-touch-hand.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple’s new MacBook Pro with PROLED XDR Display (<a href=\"https://link.amazon/B004Zr4Ml\">pre-order here</a>) includes a variety of software optimizations for touch input. But Apple says it’s “only getting started” making macOS more touch-friendly.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"mac,macbook-pro-proled-xdr,macos-27\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1076523\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/29/apple-says-its-only-getting-started-updating-macos-for-touchscreens/#more-1076523\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
