        "title": "Reddit now lets you choose between For You and Following feeds",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/29/reddit-now-lets-you-choose-between-for-you-and-following-feeds/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/10/Reddit-now-lets-you-choose-between-For-You-and-Following-feeds.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1400\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/reddit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Reddit</a> has announced the introduction of a new For You feed, an algorithmic-driven one that tries to find new communities and threads to match your interests. Fortunately, you don’t have to use it …</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apps,reddit\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1076460\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/29/reddit-now-lets-you-choose-between-for-you-and-following-feeds/#more-1076460\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
